# Anything the demo might leave behind
/tmp/
*.tmp

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Reproducible PDF build sources.
#
# The `build/` rule above exists for Python packaging artifacts. These three
# files are different: they are part of the published record, so that anyone
# with this repository can rebuild draft_final.pdf and check it against
# draft_final.sha256.
#
# Named individually rather than `!build/**` on purpose. A broad glob would also
# re-include *.aux, *.log or scratch images left behind if someone runs LaTeX
# directly inside build/, and those must never be committed. The `build/*` line
# ignores everything in the directory first, so only the three files below are
# re-admitted -- *.aux and *.log are covered by the rules above, but a stray
# image would not be.
#
# Git will not re-include a file whose parent directory is still excluded, hence
# `!build/` must come first.
!build/
build/*
!build/build.sh
!build/header.tex
!build/fixes.lua

